Architecture Hub Parent LWC – main shell, left navigation, page switching.
Reusable Child LWCs – Enterprise Dashboard, Portfolio Health, Risk & Compliance, Application Explorer, Technology Decisions, etc.
Visualization Layer – standard LWC + CSS/SVG for KPI cards, heatmaps, health bars, counts and portfolio cards; Chart.js only if complex charts are needed.
Apex Controller Layer – queries and aggregates Salesforce data; UI should not contain business calculations.
DTO / Wrapper Layer – sends normalized dashboard data from Apex to LWCs.
Salesforce Data Layer – Portfolio (TPM_Port__c), Application and other TPM objects/relationships.
Data flow: Salesforce Objects → SOQL/Aggregations → Apex → DTO → LWC → Dashboard/Charts.
Design should be reusable and data-driven, so the same architecture works for Portfolio, Risk & Compliance and future pages.
Current dummy data can later be replaced by real Apex data without redesigning the UI.
